 : 0\; } #block-34b143f7637ca2730c1c { --opacity: 100%\; --translate-x: 0px
 \; --translate-y: 0px\; --rotation: 0deg\; --scale-x: 100%\; --scale-y: 10
 0%\; --skew-x: 0deg\; --skew-y: 0deg\; --origin-x: 50%\; --origin-y: 50%\;
  --block-transform: none\; opacity: var(--opacity\, 1)\; transform: var(--
 block-transform)\; transform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } D
 iscover a simple yet powerful approach to painting by focusing on the thre
 e essential elements of successful artwork: drawing\, value\, and color. I
 n this two-day workshop\, George will guide students through the fundament
 als of composition and drawing\, including how to create a strong focal po
 int\, measure proportions accurately\, and lead the viewer's eye through a
  painting. Next\, participants will explore the critical role of value by 
 painting with only Ultramarine Blue and White\, learning how light and dar
 k relationships create depth\, form\, and visual impact. Finally\, student
 s will unlock the secrets of color harmony using only the three primary co
 lors and white\, mixing a wide range of vibrant palettes while exploring w
 arm and cool color relationships\, color temperature\, and atmospheric per
 spective. Through demonstrations and a series of color studies\, this work
 shop provides artists of all levels with practical tools for creating stro
 nger\, more confident paintings. This is an intermediate painting&nbsp\;cl
 ass. Students will be asked to bring their own material. A list of require
 d material will be provided to all students upon sign up. This class is lo
 cated in the PAC classroom.&nbsp\; Two days\, 12-4PM each day. About the T
 eacher:&nbsp\; George Scribner i s an artist\, filmmaker\, and longtime Di
 sney animator\, director\, and fine artist with more than 35 years at The 
 Walt Disney Company. Born and raised in Panama\, he directed Disney's anim
 ated feature&nbsp\; Oliver &amp\; Company &nbsp\;and has earned internatio
 nal recognition for his large-scale documentary paintings. His major commi
 ssions include creating 35 oil paintings chronicling the expansion of the 
 Panama Canal for its permanent collection and a multi-year series document
 ing the construction of Shanghai Disneyland. Through his work\, George com
 bines masterful draftsmanship\, storytelling\, and a lifelong passion for 
 painting and animation. Learn More:&nbsp\; www.scribnerart.com #block-aba7
